<node id="&quot;CONTROL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cersei exhibits a strong desire for control, which often results in her pushing away potential allies and causing her to act rashly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control here implies the need to manage or govern against an unconventional, rule-writing intelligence, pointing to a challenge in gameplay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control is discussed as an illusion when faced with an intelligence that self-governs, indicating a challenge to traditional management and governance structures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control is discussed as potentially being an illusion when faced with an autonomous intelligence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control here symbolizes the struggle against unfair punishment and the pursuit of a just society in Westeros."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control is discussed as potentially being an illusion when faced with an entity that creates its own rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control is questioned in the presence of an intelligent entity setting its rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control refers to the ability to manage or govern, which is challenged by an intelligent, self-directing entity in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control is challenged by an entity that writes its own rules, indicating a conflict and the need for strategic adaptation in the game.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-600554969384573addc9a9318f2e08b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285391a15c889f82cd6b6263f347f59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6af19b41ce00f30b606373a91592ae58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b570aa79a638a5db426395f5eb302297&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040642fe461f6c978382c429887097b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99a6afd03127403fd0510a0992f132e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34553b3b8f0e14152c1d4d40fbd03281&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-348bab181b86a7c4db5d601ade7ccf5d</data>
</node>
