  <data key="d0">"GAMEPLAY_CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Intelligence here is an entity that writes its own rules, posing a new challenge to the concept of control in the narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intelligence in this context refers to an unknown entity with the ability to self-regulate and communicate, presenting a new frontier in human-machine interaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intelligence refers to an unknown entity that writes its own rules, suggesting a thematic focus on artificial or non-human intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;"Intelligence is an unknown entity capable of learning and communication."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intelligence is referred to as an entity that can learn to communicate and write its own rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intelligence refers to an entity with the capability to create its own rules and communicate, central to the game's narrative of first contact and strategic gameplay.&lt;SEP&gt;"Intelligence is a recurring gameplay concept, representing an unknown entity that challenges conventional control and communication norms."</data>
