<node id="&quot;FIONNUALA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fionnuala agrees on music as an emotional support in games and inquires about indie games with standout scores."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala agrees on the connection between music and atmosphere in games and cites 'Gris' as an example of emotional synergy through music."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala agrees on the power of music to enhance emotional connections in games and asks for more examples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala appreciates the deep exploration of game characters and is looking forward to future discussions on this topic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is discussing the introduction of unique powers in the game, which she hopes will enhance both combat and exploration, indicating her interest in gameplay mechanics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala discusses her favorite thoroughbred horse character in the game, noting the balance of speed, stamina, and the bond formed with the horse."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala recounts a hilarious glitch where her character floats after a cutscene, adding to the light-hearted moments in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala enjoys the dynamic switching between games and apps facilitated by the PS5 Control Center, specifically appreciating the ability to adjust audio settings without pausing the gameplay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala uses post-battle periods in 'Octopath Traveler' for item collection, leveling, and experimenting with party dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala discusses her appreciation for the remastered soundtrack of 'Mass Effect Legendary Edition' and its contribution to the emotional depth of the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a commenter discussing the importance of music in video games, particularly in relation to emotional storytelling and atmosphere."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala mentions "Resident Evil 7" for its suspenseful atmosphere, with sound design and music that create a constant sense of dread and anticipation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala discusses the aftermath of a quest involving the fate of elf women, focusing on the broader impact of individual decisions in Witcher 3."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala fondly recalls a particular moment with Dandelion, appreciating his character's impact and the memorable experiences he brings to the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is actively collecting Gwent cards, appreciating both the strategic gameplay and the narrative lore they represent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala recalls a humorous moment with Dandelion during the 'A Poet Under Pressure' quest, showcasing the entertaining dynamic of their friendship."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala recalls a specific scene with Dandelion that stands out as a memorable and enjoyable part of the gameplay experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala enjoys tactical missions and discusses her favorite, "Crew Expendable," highlighting the game's tense atmosphere and storytelling prowess."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is in favor of more stealth-focused missions and suggests incorporating characters with intelligence-based gameplay for balance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala proposes a stealth-focused character with an intelligence or espionage background, imagining missions requiring strategic planning and cooperation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala recalls the "No Fighting in the War Room" mission and appreciates its unpredictable nature and emotional impact on storytelling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala suggests a gadget that creates holographic decoys to add deception and strategy to gameplay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala believes that emotional ties with NPCs make game experiences more unforgettable and significant, often influencing her to replay games with strong NPCs for the richness it adds to the storytelling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala finds that emotional ties with NPCs create unforgettable experiences and often leads to replaying games with strong NPCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala finds the surreal combination of rain and nature sounds in the forested areas particularly impactful, feeling as if the game is narrating a story through its auditory elements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala finds using Blink in 'Dishonored' game-changing for navigating and avoiding detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a gamer who enjoys stealth gameplay in 'Dishonored' and finds using the Blink ability particularly useful for navigation and avoiding detection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala recalls an unexpected dragon fight in 'Skyrim' that turned into a rewarding quest with great loot."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala shares an exciting experience in 'Skyrim' where she unexpectedly engaged in a dragon fight while on a quest."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-285391a15c889f82cd6b6263f347f59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e85fb61b77ac6d40bb3f08b419dc7e79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-147bbb5c66b3d5563be009239dd303f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb14624ae08f728624d90672e0213f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b6c70f1f1db609178bfdc91d3768a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad8b8b0237c41d579d000eb9c3b6d306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9bd620eec91e0a42f9fcde52746417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c6f55c56f67e96495c470987dcd1e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-953924359c48fae687acc00ad69285db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4da48420f35255d891d9ea7bf172f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99a6afd03127403fd0510a0992f132e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6e53ebf005461f3c0f736fe8b4dc3fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f98a3791fe103c9cf8a4adb7933c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eeb4df05dff36360ce44200ea377c4ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38431194bdc377a7a9a8a5f1b8777d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a0e37c955ed83033c9144df42611eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a3558efd338376c57831fd2b422df39</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GAVRIEL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gavriel acknowledges the well-rounded character development in Witcher 3, particularly Geralt's multifaceted relationships with others like Ciri, Yennefer, and Dandelion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel advocates for enemy types resistant to certain powers and a cooldown system for abilities, demonstrating an interest in game balance and tactical combat challenges."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is anticipating a variety of enemies with unique abilities and epic boss battles, showing his desire for strategic depth in combat."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel describes a glitch where his horse walks backwards, turning a serious mission into a comedic experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel joins the discussion, focusing on the character development and transformation of Arthur, particularly his growth in caring for his family."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel enjoys "Persona 5 Royal" for its RPG elements, social simulation, strategic battles, and beautiful art style, and inquires about characters and similar games."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel inquires about preferred combat styles, sharing his own enjoyment of planning and tactical play in turn-based games."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is willing to take risks with a full support setup in 'Octopath Traveler', depending on the context of the fight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel prefers turn-based combat and enjoys the strategic depth and planning it offers, sharing his appreciation for games where decisions significantly impact outcomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel's preference for risk with a support setup indicates a strategic approach focusing on endurance and attrition in challenging encounters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel discusses "God of War" and "Final Fantasy VII Remake", highlighting their storytelling and character development aspects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel brings up 'Final Fantasy VII Remake' for its ability to blend nostalgic themes with innovative music that heightens the intensity and emotional stakes during significant game moments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel appreciates Dandelion's role in serenading Gerald with lighthearted moments, stressing the importance of friendship in the midst of chaos, and the memorable impact of his character."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel appreciates the depth and complexity of Geralt's decisions, especially concerning characters like Ciri, and acknowledges the game's refusal to provide clear-cut answers.&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel appreciates the humorous and loyal aspects of Dandelion's character, highlighting the depth of friendship within Geralt's story."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel connects with Geralt's decisions involving Ciri, emphasizing the sense of responsibility it brings to the gameplay.&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel fondly recalls moments with Dandelion, highlighting his adventurous spirit and the friendship theme in the game.&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel reflects on the profound sense of responsibility he feels towards characters like Ciri when making decisions for Geralt, emphasizing the impact on their individual stories."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel discusses the appeal of gadgets that manipulate enemy communications and temporarily disable weapons, emphasizing the tactical importance of such tools."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel proposes a new character with tech-savvy skills to interact with modern warfare technology, suggesting potential conflicts and comedic elements.&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel shows interest in seeing classic characters like Price or Soap in modern settings, pondering their evolved stories."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel underscores the importance of gadgets that climb terrain and create distractions, enhancing the tactical dimension of gameplay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multiplayer Experience"&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel appreciates platformers like "Gris" that explore themes of grief and emotional growth through gameplay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel appreciates the emotional depth in games like 'Gris', where art and music amplify themes of grief and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel connects with Trico from 'The Last Guardian', highlighting the emotional weight and realistic behaviors of animal NPCs, and reflects on memorable animal companions in other games."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel notes the themes of grief and emotional growth in "Gris" as something more profound than the game's initial presentation suggests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel has had a memorable experience of the changing landscapes during sunrise in the mountain regions, noting the realistic snow effects and their transformative impact."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel discusses his engaging experience with the big bosses in 'Bloodborne', emphasizing the atmosphere, lore, and the challenge."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel enjoys 'The Witcher 3' for its rich quests, engaging side stories, and immersive landscapes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel finds excitement in unplanned moments such as the dragon attack in Whiterun while questing in 'Skyrim'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel recounts a thrilling moment during a dragon attack in Whiterun in 'Skyrim', feeling like a hero among townsfolk."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bbf531a9b5142506db3929de13e3a37c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-285391a15c889f82cd6b6263f347f59a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e85fb61b77ac6d40bb3f08b419dc7e79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-430e8cddee106871c8512521fbef0ce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-147bbb5c66b3d5563be009239dd303f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb14624ae08f728624d90672e0213f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-295e2ee40671a699f134d711e7a02a1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b6c70f1f1db609178bfdc91d3768a93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad8b8b0237c41d579d000eb9c3b6d306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c9bd620eec91e0a42f9fcde52746417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-168252cb122d05b62333573b92a01ca5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4da48420f35255d891d9ea7bf172f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99a6afd03127403fd0510a0992f132e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6e53ebf005461f3c0f736fe8b4dc3fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6f98a3791fe103c9cf8a4adb7933c89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a0e37c955ed83033c9144df42611eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a3558efd338376c57831fd2b422df39</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENEMY ENCOUNTERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Enemy encounters refer to the different types of adversaries that might require various strategies, suggesting a focus on the combat system's complexity."</data>
