</node>
<node id="&quot;JARETH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Jareth admires the realism in 'Red Dead Redemption 2', especially the interactions at the camp and the evolving narrative nature of the camp's setup."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth also appreciates moments of relaxation and exploration after intense gameplay in 'Octopath Traveler'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth enjoys the excitement and preparation involved in boss fights in 'Octopath Traveler', and the epic atmosphere they create."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth is experimenting with character skills in 'Octopath Traveler' and seeking out successful team combos."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth is interested in creative combat tactics and the implementation of a combo system where abilities combine for enhanced effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth shares a surreal experience of being stuck in a fence, highlighting the humorous mishaps encountered in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth shares their experience with a side mission involving local townsfolk, focusing on how it deepens Arthur's character portrayal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth discusses the depth added to the gameplay experience by "The Witcher 3" and its storytelling, and his interest in "Detroit: Become Human" for its thought-provoking themes.&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth enjoys the immersive storytelling of "The Witcher 3" and "Ghost of Tsushima", focusing on themes of honor, sacrifice, and the impact of choices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth is curious about other games that reshape understanding of themes like identity and history through branching narratives."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth prefers co-op gameplay, enjoys teaming up with friends for challenging missions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth enjoys "Firewatch" for its use of music to deepen the relationship between characters Henry and Delilah, creating an intimate and emotionally resonant experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth is interested in games that effectively connect music with atmosphere, specifically mentioning 'Hollow Knight'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth engages in strategic revision after losses, analyzing what went wrong to improve his deck and gameplay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth enjoys the storyline involving the Bloody Baron and acknowledges the emotional impact of the character's personal struggles and choices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth suggests revisiting 'Mass Effect' for its impactful character relationships influenced by player choices, and 'The Witcher 3' for deeply layered companion interactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth appreciates the evolving camp in 'Red Dead Redemption 2' and the unforgettable moments from campfire conversations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jareth discusses using the Leviathan Axe's freezing ability to his advantage in 'God of War'."</data>
