<node id="&quot;KIERAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Kieran adds to the discussion by speculating on character development, particularly the possibility of Maeve leading a rebellion against humans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran appreciates the theme of vulnerability and the importance of supportive relationships among friends, which enriches the narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran appreciates the thrilling and unpredictable nature of character development in the series, particularly Kendall's arc."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran further emphasizes the excitement surrounding the character development and the suspense in future plot twists for Kendall's evolution within the narrative."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran inquires about Kendall's potential to break free from the influence of his childhood rivalry with Logan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran is enthusiastic about the character development and the rollercoaster-like storyline of the episodes, looking forward to more plot twists."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran's response is not present, but implied engagement as they are invited to share their vote at the end of the conversation.&lt;SEP&gt;"The mention of Kieran's pending vote suggests his active participation in the discussion despite the lack of a direct statement, indicating engagement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran wonders if Cersei had moments of doubt and specifically inquires about her dynamic with Jaime Lannister."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran believes strong relationships can serve as a grounding force, potentially preventing characters from making poor moral choices.&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran is in favor of stories with morally ambiguous characters, mentioning how they reflect real-life struggles and growth, making them compelling for viewers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran is intrigued by the evolution of characters such as Jimmy in "Better Call Saul," who navigate a path toward moral decline through their decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran likes how "Stranger Things" showcases the power of friendship in overcoming challenges and adversity, and how it strengthens the bond between characters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran recognizes the testing of friendships as both a unifying and challenging force, which is crucial in depicting characters' growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kieran sees the message that vulnerability and facing fears together is strength in unity, which he believes viewers take away as a positive reflection on interpersonal relationships."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-175fe4cd2357d08bc7abcb88ff85e3cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c5e5f4bb7bbe2044095b40d65eca145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-432b50669e408b7cc1df78b2d7d5c9ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2d4a40a78adcd43333ae04eb46fe71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b06d4d3a137930f1d7ee5992f939c4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c5f78717906d8ae6fd13d75f1b449de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3940135ac87c476b983437ffff34e3a</data>
</node>
